<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1"><strong>Mid-Level Ques=
tions:</strong></h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q3: Explain the differen=
ce between module.hot.accept() and module.hot.decline()</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Expected Answer:</strong=
></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>accept():</strong> Modu=
le agrees to handle hot updates</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>decline():</strong> Mod=
ule refuses hot updates, triggers fallback (usually page reload)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Use cases:</strong> Dec=
line for modules that cannot be safely updated (database connections, criti=
cal configuration)</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Advanced Follow-up:</str=
ong>
<em>"In what scenarios would you programmatically call module.hot.decline()=
 based on runtime conditions?"</em></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q4: Why doesn't mini-css=
-extract-plugin work v=E1=BB=9Bi HMR?</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Expected Answer:</strong=
></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>mini-css-extract-plugin=
:</strong> Extracts CSS to separate files during build time</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>HMR requirement:</stron=
g> CSS needs to be injectable at runtime</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Solution:</strong> Use =
style-loader trong development, mini-css-extract-plugin trong production</l=
i>
</ul>
